# @NAME@ (C64): reconstructed source

A Kick Assembler reconstruction of this Commodore 64 game. Status: **phase 1, just started.** It follows the shared process in the `c64-decomp` skill (`references/new_game.md`).

**No game binary is in this repository** (`reference.sha256` holds the SHA-256 the build is checked against). You supply the original media and derive the reference yourself.

## What you need
Linux or macOS; Java 17+ and Kick Assembler; VICE with its C64 ROMs and `c1541`; `just`; Python 3; `gcc`; Ghidra 11+ with the `ghidra-kickass-export` script in `~/ghidra_scripts`; the `c64-decomp` skill (`~/.claude/skills/c64-decomp`, or set `C64_DECOMP`). `just env` checks them.

## Supplying the data
Put the media in `originals/` (read-only, with their SHA-256 in `originals.sha256`; **never attach an original to an emulator directly**: VICE writes disk images back).

## Deriving the reference and building
    just derive      # dumps from a scratch copy of the medium, vote out loader noise, decrunch in the tracer, write reference/
    just verify      # assemble phase1/src and check it is byte-identical to the reference
    just seeds       # coverage run in the tracer, then Ghidra seeds from what executed
    just ghidra      # import into Ghidra and export to ghidra/ (the landing zone; phase1/src is hand-edited from the first seeding on)
`just --list` shows everything. Background research: `docs/background.md`; boot analysis: `docs/boot_analysis.md`.

---

Decompiled with [MOSaic](https://github.com/Dave-Agent/MOSaic) (MOS AI deCompiler).
